**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Each slot's role on the light path, read from the one ray law: Source, Prep 1…k, Object 1…n, Analyzer 1…k and Detector (001 §J 'Source, Prep 1…k, Object 1…n (two or more samples in series), Analyzer 1…k, Detector'; the S8.2 brief's slot roles; AGENTS.md 'One ray law for every element'). The role is derived from the slot's kind and where the light reaches it, never stored, so sliding an element past a sample changes its role with no second source of truth. In `Setups.fs`, after `Setup` (step 256), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) `SlotPosition of int` with `.value`, a slot's 1-based place within its role. (2) `SlotRole` = `SourceSlotRole` | `PrepSlotRole of SlotPosition` | `ObjectSlotRole of SlotPosition` | `AnalyzerSlotRole of SlotPosition` | `DetectorSlotRole of SlotPosition`, with `member this.text : string` = `Source`, `Prep <k>`, `Obj <k>`, `Analyzer <k>` or `Detector <k>` (001 §J's chip names). A role is never stored, so it carries no wire tag. (3) `RoledSlot = { role : SlotRole; slot : SetupSlot }`. (4) `type SetupSlot with static member inLightOrder (slots : SetupSlot list) : RoledSlot list` lays the slots out with `BeamLayout.layout` (`BeamLayout.fs:layout`) over their `layoutElement`s (step 256), the first slot being the ray root, and reads each slot's laid-out `path` (`BeamLayout.fs:PlacedElement`): its light depth is the number of steps of that path. A `LightSource` slot is the source; a `Sample` slot is an object; a `Detector` slot is a detector; any other slot is a prep when no step of its path is a `Sample` slot (the light reaches it before any object) and an analyzer otherwise, an element on an object's reflected ray included. Within each role the slots are ordered by light depth and then by table order, and numbered from 1, so Obj 1 is the sample the light crosses first and a second sample in series is Obj 2. The answer lists the sources, then the preps, the objects, the analyzers and the detectors. A slot the layout does not place (its host's reflected ray is off, say) has an empty path (`BeamLayout.fs:layoutWith`) and keeps its kind's role, ordered after the placed slots of that role. (5) `type Setup with member this.lightOrder : RoledSlot list` is `SetupSlot.inLightOrder this.slots`. No other member is added. Tests, in `SetupTests` (step 256), over test-local slot lists in table order whose x positions lie between `RayModel.defaultSourcePoint` and `RayModel.defaultDetectorPoint`. `a setup's slots take their roles in light order: the source, the preps, the objects in series, the analyzers, the detectors`: the slots `src`, `det`, `lpA` (x −0.3 m), `sampleB` (x 0.1 m), `sampleA` (x −0.1 m) and `lpB` (x 0.3 m), all on the main beam, answer `src` Source, `lpA` Prep 1, `sampleA` Obj 1, `sampleB` Obj 2, `lpB` Analyzer 1 and `det` Detector 1, in that order. `an element behind an object, on its reflected ray included, is an analyzer, and without an object every optical element is a prep`: with `sampleA` emitting both branches (`EmitBoth`), the same slots plus `polR` (a `LinearPolarizer` at x 0.2 m) and `detR` (a `Detector` at x 0.5 m), both on `OnReflectedBeamOf sampleA`, answer `polR` Analyzer 1 (its path src, lpA, sampleA is three steps) before `lpB` Analyzer 2 (four), and `detR` Detector 1 (four) before `det` Detector 2 (five); and the slots `src`, `lp1` (x −0.3 m), `lp2` (x 0.2 m) and `det` with no sample answer Source, Prep 1, Prep 2 and Detector 1. `a role renders its chip name`: `SourceSlotRole`, `PrepSlotRole (SlotPosition 2)`, `ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)`, `AnalyzerSlotRole (SlotPosition 3)` and `DetectorSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)` render `Source`, `Prep 2`, `Obj 1`, `Analyzer 3` and `Detector 1`.

**Acceptance.** After the roles land, `SetupSlot.inLightOrder` and `Setup.lightOrder` MUST give each slot its role from its kind and its laid-out path, objects in series numbered in light order; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a setup's slots take their roles in light order: the source, the preps, the objects in series, the analyzers, the detectors`, `an element behind an object, on its reflected ray included, is an analyzer, and without an object every optical element is a prep` and `a role renders its chip name`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
